{
	"name": "CombatHud",
	"_doc": "The combat HUD (Config/Hud; src/client/HudKit builds it, src/client/AmmoHud, StaffHud and ArtilleryHud fill it). No panels or backgrounds (user 2026-10-26): each cut-away (`model`, a ViewportFrame) floats over the game, the gun's at the bottom right, the staff's rock in the same place, the artillery crew's at the bottom centre; one shows at a time. Sizes in reference pixels at theme.scale.referenceHeight, one UIScale. Colours are Config/Palette UI.Hud names. The gun's cut-away is two layers (user 2026-10-26: \"make everything else just a simple shadow sillouette\"): GunShadow, the gun's body as one flat see-through shadow, under GunView, the clear bolt, rounds and magazine well (a child draws over its parent). Desktop only. The kit list (`Kit`, src/client/KitList, Config/Hud.Kit; user 2026-10-27: \"make it a kit list but move it on the left\"): one `KitRow` per item carried this life, cloned from the template and stacked upward from the bottom left (a UIListLayout, Config/Hud.Kit.gap); each row bare ink (UI overhaul, user 2026-10-30: \"remove the paper background completely, just have the selected one be fully visible and the others semi transparent and smaller\"): the plate and the key's stamp stay clear, the key, the name in capitals and a count as words with a dark edge; the row in the hands full and larger, the others smaller and see-through (Config/Hud.Kit). The gun's hint (`Hint`): the key as a red chip, then what it does (RichText). The gunner's warning (`ArtilleryWarn`, src/client/ArtilleryHud; user 2026-11-02: \"put the warning more center bottom/top of the screen so players know\"): why the gun can't fire where it's laid, in the bottom centre.",
